n1. Autism Speaks 2023 Annual Report (Autism by the Numbers): https://www.autismspeaks.org/sites/default/files/ABN_Annual_Report_2023.pdf\n2. U.S. Census Bureau, American Community Survey 2023 1-Year Estimates, Poverty Status in the Past 12 Months: https://www2.census.gov/library/publications/2024/demo/acsbr-022.pdf\n\n**Note:** The Autism Speaks data shows West Virginia has the oldest average age (7.2 years) but ranks 2nd in poverty. Mississippi has the highest poverty rate (18.0%) among these 10 states but ranks 5th in intervention age. Colorado has both the joint-youngest intervention age among the 10 (5.0 years) and the lowest poverty rate (9.3%)."}]}}
